// Antifrost — the searched wing: five hills written for the short wake.
//
// Legend: `#` rock, `,` dirt, `.` tunnel, `@` player start,
// uppercase `W R Y G B` beds (W is the player's), lowercase `r y g b` wild ants.
//
// Every hill here carries `wake: "short"`, which is a different physics,
// not a different map: the line remembers only as many steps as it has
// ants, and a new recruit takes the place nearest the player instead of the
// deepest one. The wake lock, the last-in-first-warm peel, the bunching, the
// leave-behind, the dunk and the bed-walls all still apply — what changes is
// that no action can carry an ant further than one cell, and therefore the
// farthest thing still owed a place is a true lower bound on the moves left.
//
// That is the whole point of the wing. Under the long wake of the hills
// above, a collect re-slots an ant down a road walked long ago, so no
// distance bounds the moves remaining, IDA* has nothing to prune on, and a
// par can only be had by walking the hill exhaustively — which is why seven
// of them are still "beatable, not claimed unbeatable". Here the
// bound holds, so `solver::ida_star` proves these five instead of hunting
// them: par is the optimum, and the proof costs a path's memory rather than
// a layer's.
//
// Par policy: all five carry their IDA* optimum. The first four are also
// settled by exhaustive BFS as a cross-check, so those pars are numbers two
// independent searches agree on; the fifth outruns the arena a test session
// carries, and IDA* is what proves it. `solver::tests::solve_all_short_wake`
// re-runs both (it is `#[ignore]`d for the usual patience reason); the tests
// that DO run every session replay these five routes move by move and check
// the bound never once overshoots along them.
//
// The five are a ladder. `First Light` is the wake itself: step off a bed
// and the ant at your heels falls into it. `The Alcove` adds the one bed the
// wake can never reach, which has to be dunked. `Heel Marks` is the stack —
// whoever was picked up last is warmed first, so the two bunks are visited
// in the order that says so. `Two Warm Walls` makes two of the beds into
// walls on the way out, so the hill's own answers block it. `Ash Hall` is
// all of it at once on a longer road — three ants, a wall down the middle,
// a bunk in a pocket that only the dunk reaches, and the leave-behind as the
// only way to sort the line.
//
// `Ash Hall` is also the argument for the whole wing. Its optimum is forty
// moves; exhaustive BFS needs an arena of four hundred million states to
// settle it, which is not a thing a test session — let alone a pocket — can
// carry, and at the cap this suite runs under BFS simply does not answer.
// IDA* answers, in a path's worth of memory, because `wake_bound` is telling
// the truth about how far is left. Same proof, two currencies.

(
    levels: [
        (
            name: "First Light",
            wake: "short",
            par: 6,
            grid: [
                "#########",
                "#...R...#",
                "#..r..W.#",
                "#..@....#",
                "#########",
            ],
        ),
        (
            name: "The Alcove",
            wake: "short",
            par: 11,
            grid: [
                "##########",
                "#......###",
                "#..y....Y#",
                "#..@..W###",
                "##########",
            ],
        ),
        (
            name: "Heel Marks",
            wake: "short",
            par: 14,
            grid: [
                "##########",
                "#.R....Y.#",
                "#..r..y..#",
                "#...@...W#",
                "##########",
            ],
        ),
        (
            name: "Two Warm Walls",
            wake: "short",
            par: 25,
            grid: [
                "############",
                "#R........Y#",
                "#.r......y.#",
                "#....@.....#",
                "#####W######",
            ],
        ),
        (
            name: "Ash Hall",
            wake: "short",
            par: 40,
            grid: [
                "##############",
                "#@.....#.....#",
                "#....y.#..Y..#",
                "#......#.....#",
                "#..g...#.....#",
                "#......#####b#",
                "#.G.....W...B#",
                "##############",
            ],
        ),
    ],
)
